. 
.         * As seen from the described variables, our model aims to test whethe
> r the household home work,
.         * approximated as the proportion of hours spent on childcare and home
> work, is more equally distributed 
.         * in the families with daughters. The distribution of the work at the
>  household is constructed for each of the partners, 
.         * and then the percentage of the total domestic work is calculated, s
> erving as a dependent variable. 
.         * The daughter variable is then being used as the key independent var
> iable. 
.         * Given the nature of the dependent variable, we can this time opt fo
> r simple OLS regression with household and family controls. *
. 
